{"lines":[{"x":0.15963228118675266,"y":0.067999653330245602,"t":"Test 1","w":0.058554986317952473,"c":1,"h":0.016616972354021819},{"h":0.022406620435843738,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","y":0.11529440202268759,"c":1,"x":0.15756760714297732,"w":0.29764475504557286},{"x":0.15755432716084897,"y":0.1530245056176025,"w":0.78450871785481779,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","h":0.030088192558411331,"c":1},{"y":0.17151162786057994,"x":0.1560150381079897,"t":"Passage 3 below.","w":0.1635338338216146,"h":0.020375042981051306,"c":1},{"x":0.44895792274887308,"y":0.2149354679326998,"w":0.20362780253092444,"h":0.022850746503585651,"c":1,"t":"Artificial artists"},{"h":0.025802409656571212,"c":1,"t":"Can computers really create works of art?","x":0.31361912170065426,"y":0.25129245567187408,"w":0.4779661560058594},{"c":1,"t":"The Painting Fool is one of a growing number of computer programs which, so their","h":0.026431137104611646,"w":0.74677088419596349,"x":0.15384113415091452,"y":0.28941621230387282},{"c":1,"x":0.15382787920283741,"t":"makers claim, possess creative talents. Classical music by an artificial composer has","w":0.75814331054687489,"h":0.030467193662467751,"y":0.30577975913918976},{"h":0.025643953567770161,"c":1,"t":"had audiences enraptured, and even tricked them into believing a human was behind","x":0.15199286576423759,"y":0.32669972628997512,"w":0.76175394694010401},{"y":0.34480415421845612,"h":0.025953262142419664,"c":1,"t":"the score. Artworks painted by a robot have sold for thousands of dollars and been hung","x":0.15011057800445543,"w":0.78814239501953121},{"y":0.36409633424219234,"x":0.15015747637336044,"w":0.74854482014973955,"c":1,"h":0.022707254442950742,"t":"in prestigious galleries. And software has been built which creates art that could not"},{"w":0.36746462504069016,"t":"have been imagined by the programmer.","c":1,"y":0.37969716104420748,"x":0.14994726992195334,"h":0.025158628523925586},{"t":"Human beings are the only species to perform sophisticated creative acts regularly.","c":1,"h":0.026265563768336553,"x":0.15008207065252946,"y":0.41742616223692663,"w":0.74496444702148445},{"h":0.026645703386354747,"x":0.14816901587060016,"y":0.43609300702837617,"t":"If we can break this process down into computer code, where does that leave human","c":1,"w":0.75998143513997407},{"y":0.45168294811956056,"t":"creativity? 'This is a question at the very core of humanity,' says Geraint Wiggins, a","x":0.14825294712190243,"c":1,"h":0.028674779672125283,"w":0.74116694132486971},{"c":1,"y":0.47315683868955738,"t":"computational creativity researcher at Goldsmiths, University of London. 'It scares a lot","h":0.025075394187676681,"w":0.77669148763020823,"x":0.14831478681100643},{"h":0.028339997615187906,"x":0.14821845361651007,"c":1,"y":0.49016624787433449,"w":0.77687240600585927,"t":"of people. They are worried that it is taking something special away from what it means"},{"c":1,"x":0.14653356745951565,"w":0.12798549652099608,"t":"to be human.'","h":0.018182108498970617,"y":0.50980429457117116},{"y":0.54640720115039554,"c":1,"t":"To some extent, we are all familiar with computerised art. The question is: where does","x":0.14822237634598592,"w":0.76554138183593756,"h":0.024848120026794152},{"w":0.77870936075846364,"h":0.024828034528055598,"y":0.56524193789410238,"c":1,"x":0.1463376004811974,"t":"the work of the artist stop and the creativity of the computer begin? Consider one of the"},{"w":0.77485967000325506,"t":"oldest machine artists, Aaron, a robot that has had paintings exhibited in London's Tate","x":0.1463966402064088,"y":0.58387587974486543,"h":0.025232453846731895,"c":1},{"t":"Modern and the San Francisco Museum of Modern Art. Aaron can pick up a paintbrush","x":0.14634898675646876,"y":0.60038331451029991,"c":1,"w":0.77498377482096359,"h":0.026813180386751512},{"y":0.61964365323829995,"h":0.026431187459598049,"c":1,"w":0.78998972574869786,"t":"and paint on canvas on its own. Impressive perhaps, but it is still little more than a tool to","x":0.14636100662355697},{"t":"realise the programmer's own creative ideas.","y":0.63740615104882259,"w":0.40654322306315105,"h":0.022569898321639359,"x":0.14448953203041459,"c":1},{"h":0.025224580046290801,"c":1,"x":0.14448488928420375,"y":0.67430437776919128,"t":"Simon Colton, the designer of the Painting Fool, is keen to make sure his creation","w":0.72982238769531249},{"w":0.79011347452799485,"x":0.14441746084506565,"h":0.033233765395165094,"t":"doesn't attract the same criticism. Unlike earlier 'artists' such as Aaron, the Painting Fool","c":1,"y":0.68758029905823592},{"c":1,"t":"only needs minimal direction and can come up with its own concepts by going online for","y":0.71142162814693166,"x":0.14450492214394189,"w":0.78428639729817706,"h":0.025573737837772503},{"w":0.78800699869791657,"x":0.14269782710140949,"t":"material. The software runs its own web searches and trawls through social media sites.","y":0.73025834485161789,"h":0.024376170986787127,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.026971150120073784,"t":"It is now beginning to display a kind of imagination too, creating pictures from scratch.","x":0.14257483634347068,"y":0.74749915749399098,"w":0.76750920613606766},{"w":0.77122706095377591,"t":"One of its original works is a series of fuzzy landscapes, depicting trees and sky. While","y":0.76666548542295943,"h":0.025544853726280792,"c":1,"x":0.14444226295099999},{"x":0.1407886845839125,"w":0.76546895345052102,"t":"some might say they have a mechanical look, Colton argues that such reactions arise","y":0.78480657141364207,"c":1,"h":0.024675142051171162},{"x":0.14071347956035918,"w":0.73351918538411454,"y":0.8036454704316206,"t":"from people's double standards towards software-produced and human-produced","h":0.024535698040178078,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.024901194182504693,"y":0.82201287773854204,"t":"art. After all, he says, consider that the Painting Fool painted the landscapes without","x":0.1407763382299197,"w":0.75415654500325524},{"x":0.14070862651106192,"y":0.83900438931317789,"w":0.74302286783854177,"t":"referring to a photo. 'If a child painted a new scene from its head, you'd say it has a","h":0.026717537844941019,"c":1},{"y":0.858226897294183,"c":1,"w":0.74283950805664067,"x":0.14077071574035718,"h":0.024173220740697166,"t":"certain level of imagination,' he points out. 'The same should be true of a machine.'"},{"w":0.710968017578125,"t":"Software bugs can also lead to unexpected results. Some of the Painting Fool's","y":0.8773600575006516,"x":0.14073357875860193,"h":0.024468932240836794,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.14075197626970712,"w":0.77487986246744789,"h":0.025702332191442689,"t":"paintings of a chair came out in black and white, thanks to a technical glitch. This gives","y":0.89505992648180954},{"w":0.78054102579752604,"y":0.91415988804738169,"x":0.13885593769955032,"c":1,"h":0.024607322481625782,"t":"the work an eerie, ghostlike quality. Human artists like the renowned Ellsworth Kelly are"},{"y":0.93239728256848453,"w":0.73920008341471344,"h":0.024975509545301033,"c":1,"t":"lauded for limiting their colour palette - so why should computers be any different?","x":0.13696526983250285},{"w":0.026315789222717295,"x":0.13721804515282451,"h":0.013081395234588844,"c":1,"t":"24","y":0.96947674418370988}],"w":2400,"h":3106}